     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §5, Chap 672 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4069\n\nSPONSOR: BORRELLO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993, amending the public\nauthorities law relating to the construction and financing of facilities\nfor certain public libraries, in relation to including the Olean Public\nLibrary\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend chapter 672 of the laws of 1993, amending the public authori-\nties law relating to the construction and financing of facilities for\npublic libraries, in relation to including the Olean Public Library.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmending the public authorities law relating to the construction and\nfinancing facilities for certain public libraries, in relation to\nincluding the Olean Public Library.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPublic libraries are centers for the community and allow citizens of all\nages to immerse themselves in knowledge. With the usage of financial\nagencies such as DASNY, a low cost, large issuer of tax-exempt municipal\nbonds, it allows public libraries to economically fund renovation and\nrelocation projects.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
